{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The fat that covers the entrails.</b> It is the membrane over the paunch — which they call טי״לא." "<b>And the appendage.</b> It is the טַרְפְּשָׁא דְכַבְדָא — which they call איבר״יש." "<b>Upon the liver.</b> From the liver too take along with it (Sifra)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French tieule, a membrane or caul", 1 "the Aramaic is literally 'the webbing of the liver'; the la'az is Old French iverée or a similar term for liver-appendage"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:29.639023391Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}